      "title": "Mixed option spellings bypass the fixed execution_01 guard",
      "finding": "The wrapper counts only argv elements exactly equal to --execution-directory. A vector containing one exact canonical pair and a later --execution-directory=/tmp/s47-c2-bypass element passes that guard. The inherited argparse parser accepts both spellings and retains the later alternate path, so parent(args) creates and uses a noncanonical receipt directory despite the protocol's fixed execution_01 requirement.",
      "evidence": "Independent standard-library reproduction returned wrapper_accepts_duplicate_mixed_spelling=true and inherited_argparse_effective_execution_directory=/tmp/s47-c2-bypass.",
      "required_fix": "Parse the effective arguments before enforcing the path, reject duplicate option occurrences across both argparse spellings, and require the single parsed execution_directory to resolve exactly to execution_01 in both parent and internal worker routes. Add negative tests for mixed spellings and ordering."
    },
    {
      "id": "S47-C2-SOURCE-BLOCKER-002",
      "severity": "BLOCKER",
      "file": "/Users/rocket/Desktop/HKUST IT/ip-/geometry-world-modeling/work/S47_c2_confirmation_generation/launch_generation.py",
      "lines": [
        136,
        149
      ],
      "parent_file": "/Users/rocket/Desktop/HKUST IT/ip-/geometry-world-modeling/work/S35_generation_integration/launch_original.py",
      "parent_lines": [
        449,
        460
      ],
      "title": "External --worker dispatch can bypass the monitored parent route",
      "finding": "The outer wrapper validates only the execution-directory token and does not reject --worker. The inherited main dispatches directly to worker(args) when that flag is present. After authorization, a caller can create the chosen execution directory and a matching launch_ticket using its own parent PID and the public launcher/manifest hashes, then enter the full gate/runtime/generation path without the parent process-tree monitor and its external limit enforcement.",
      "evidence": "Independent standard-library parsing returned wrapper_accepts_external_worker_flag=true and inherited_argparse_dispatches_worker=true; source inspection confirmed that the disk ticket is composed only of caller-observable values and parent PID equality.",
      "required_fix": "Make the public entry incapable of selecting worker mode directly and authenticate internal worker dispatch to the live monitored parent, while preserving an independently testable create-only execution_01 invariant. Add a negative external --worker test before re-review."
    }
